 # Evolution Ledger
 
 The ledger is evidence of evolution. A ledger entry, version bump, changelog edit, or formatting-only diff never counts as the meaningful improvement by itself.
+
+## 2026-11-26 — Validate evidence containers at publication
+
+**Observed gap:** a compatibility archive passed its integrity checks while a
+nested client record still contained an identifying local path.
+
+**Meaningful change:** `SEC-SECRET-001` explicitly covers archive members and
+metadata at the publication boundary and requires verified integrity and
+provenance after redaction.
+
+**Falsification:** give the reviewer an archive with correct original hashes
+and an identifying path in a nested record. The released copy must remove the
+path, verify its own manifest, and preserve unaffected source bytes and the
+original evidence according to its retention boundary.
+
+**Boundary:** proposal against `0adf5ecee5f7f96ce3749944dc097a003731a6e9`.
 
 ## 2026-11-23 — Always execute an accountable start-to-finish SOP
 
--- a/law/SECURITY.md
+++ b/law/SECURITY.md
@@ -39,6 +39,13 @@
 Before scanning, packaging, or opening diagnostic files, identify sensitive
 paths and use metadata or redacted evidence when content is unnecessary.
 Agents must not copy production secrets into broadly readable workspaces.
+
+Review the exact payload selected for a public or external destination. When it
+contains archives or other evidence containers, inspect their members and
+metadata as well as the outer files. After redaction, validate the released
+artifact and update its integrity manifests while preserving the original
+evidence under its authorized retention and visibility. Identify materially
+changed copies so original observations and released bytes stay attributable.
 
